indicators.description:
This indicator measures number of girls and women who receive services related to harmful practices (HP), including child early and forced marriage and female genital mutilation (FGM), with support from the UN. GBV services are also included under this indicator. 

Number of girls at risk of or affected by child, early and forced marriage who receive, with support from United Nations, prevention and/or protection services and care related to child, early and forced marriage.

This indicator is calculated as a simple count of number of girls who received at least one of the following prevention, protection and care services with the support of United Nations:
1.        Life skills programmes (cognitive skills, personal skills and interpersonal skills);
2.        Comprehensive Sexuality Education (CSE) or health information
3.        Support to enrolment and retention in formal and non-formal education;
4.        Financial literacy and savings;
5.        Referrals to essential services, including health care, justice and social services.

This indicator is calculated as a simple count of the number of girls and women who received at least one of the following prevention/protection/care services related to female genital mutilation with the support of United Nations:
6.        Prevention: Health, education, and social services;
7.        Protection: Legal, shelters;
8.        Care: Medical, psycho-social care;
9.        Non-formal and formal education on FGM and rights issues.

indicators.title:
Number of gender-responsive, conflict-sensitive development institutions, policies, plans, or crossborder initiatives in place, with UN's support, that promote and protect human rights and prevent systemic human rights violations to: 
a) Address conflict drivers; 
b) Strengthen social cohesion; 
c) Prevent risk of conflict, including climate security; and 
d) End all forms of violence, promote the rule of law and ensure equal access to justice for all

Extent that measures developed/implemented with UN's support are in place to advance women and girl's leadership and equal participation in decision-making in: 
a) Public institutions; 
b) Elected positions, including parliaments and local governments; 
c) Judiciary; 
d) Private sector; 
e) Mediation, reconciliation and peacebuilding mechanisms; and
f) Natural resource management
